On the south side of the Le Morne peninsula, between Le Morne village and Baie du Cap, La Prairie is a long public beach with a wide strip of grass behind the sand and the profile of Le Morne Brabant to the northwest.

There are no hotels here and very few facilities, which is its charm. At weekends Mauritian families come to picnic on the grass; on weekdays it is often almost empty. The lagoon in front is shallow and calm on most days.

## Good to know

- Bring water, food and shade: there is little on site.
- The south coast is more exposed to the wind than the west; on breezy days, swim close to shore.
